# This project's entire value proposition is byte-identical output, so a
# checkout that silently rewrites line endings is a correctness hazard,
# not a cosmetic one. Without this file, fixtures/minimal-rect/expected.pdf
# contains no NUL byte and is therefore classified as text by git's
# default binary heuristic — a checkout under core.autocrlf=true (the
# Git-for-Windows default) would rewrite its LF bytes to CRLF, silently
# changing its SHA-256 out from under the normative hash recorded in
# expected.json. This story's QA review (Major 10) measured this directly
# with `git diff --numstat`, which reported line counts rather than "- -"
# for expected.pdf before this file existed.

* text=auto eol=lf

fixtures/**/*.pdf binary
fixtures/**/*.json text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf

# lint/testdata/ holds Story 1.3's licence-check fixture module graphs
# (D-1.3.8, AC30) — obviously-fake stub modules under example.test/,
# never real third-party code, marked vendored so GitHub's language
# detection and diff/review tooling do not treat them as ordinary
# repository source.
lint/testdata/** linguist-vendored
